Alongside new betas of iOS 27.2, iPadOS 27.2, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS Golden Gate</a> 27.2, Apple has released the first betas of watchOS 27.2, tvOS 27.2, and visionOS 27.2. The betas come two days after the 27.0 software updates were released.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-999927" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/04/General-visionOS-watchOS-and-tvOS-Betas-Feature-Redux.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" /><br/>
Registered developers can download the betas through the Settings app on each device.<br/>
<br/>
Two new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> features are coming to the Apple Watch Series 12 and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-watch-ultra/">Apple Watch Ultra 4</a> in late 2026, and Apple could start testing them as soon as watchOS 27.2. Live Rewind will allow users to double-press the Digital Crown to get a transcription of what was said in the last 15 seconds, while <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> Recap will turn conversations users have had during the day into high-level notes.<br/>
<br/>
